{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow","id":1506452,"title":"Basing Courts on the Colors of Rainbow","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-25T20:33:54-07:00","id":1506452,"title":"Basing Courts on the Colors of Rainbow","content":"Basically, I am hoping to set up a sci fi campaign involving Changeling: tL. It would be set on a recently settled planet, as in less than two hundred years ago. <br /> <br /> I want more than four courts so I thought of good old Roy G Biv. I'm looking for feedback and ideas.<br /> <br /> So far I assume each color court is built around two emotions. <br /> <br /> <b>RED: </b>Anger and Zeal<br /> <br /> <b>ORANGE: </b>\u200bAmbition and Contempt<br /> <br /> <b>YELLOW: </b>Curiosity and Fear<br /> <br /> <b>GREEN:</b> Love and Jealousy <br /> <br /> <b>BLUE: </b>Sorrow and Joy<br /> <br /> <b>INDIGO: </b>Wonder and ?<br /> <br /> <b>VIOLET: </b>? and ?<br /> <br /> As you can see the concept needs work.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T20:41:26-07:00","id":1506454,"title":"","content":"Indigo tends to get spiritual connotations when used in religious contexts, so... Faith, maybe? The gentle kind, in contrast to Zeal<br /> <br /> Violet tends to have associations with royalty or high rank, so... Vanity and <s>ambition</s> Greed, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-26-2023, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T20:44:27-07:00","id":1506455,"title":"","content":"What are the pairs based upon, though? Just ones that tend to accompany each other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T06:47:55-07:00","id":1506477,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend refining the concept of the patrons further to actually get a symbolset going, much like the Directional Courts draw symbolism from the Four Auspicious Beasts or the Leafless Tree's Bargain with Retaliation manifests in ways appropriate to the frontier justice it's built on. Colors are incredibly broad as symbolism to the point where most of the time you see it in cultural symbolism it's just the symbol for a different referent like Death or Marriage or The Sea.<br /> <br /> Depending on what scale of involvement &quot;takes place on a newly settled planet&quot; entails (i.e. whether the whole story takes place in different parts of the same planet for a novel setting or is instead one locale among many in a spacefaring travelogue), it may be prudent to consider how you want the distribution of courts to go \u2014 a setup where almost every freehold on the planet has all seven courts is going to be very different from one where each court is more or less geographically associated and the courts in a given freehold are determined by territorial overlap and diplomacy, which in turn is different from a unified body of changelings whose courtier are assigned to locations based on theme/mood/need/whim.<br /> <br /> It's also worth asking what &quot;sci fi campaign involving Changeling&quot; means for the larger context of adapting the base material \u2014 is this still a situation where changelings are hidden monsters coming together to share strategies for coping with the fallout of their durances, is it a more broadly applied use of Changeling's material to make weird alien cultures, or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Forgot to finish a sentence 03-26-2023, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T08:26:21-07:00","id":1506484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow?p=1506455#post1506455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the pairs based upon, though? Just ones that tend to accompany each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had trouble coming up with a good logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T12:03:13-07:00","id":1506512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow?p=1506484#post1506484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had trouble coming up with a good logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>One Vice and one Virtue -or at least one generally positive and one generally negative- per color is probably good, and youve already generally got that. Just look up the New Age associations for each color, that's probably the simplest way to justify why they lumped them together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T17:29:29-07:00","id":1506553,"title":"","content":"I still don't know what to pair with <b>Wonder.</b><br /> <br /> For <b>Violet</b> what do people think about Compassion and Disgust? They're an interesting pair and would make an interesting dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T17:36:52-07:00","id":1506556,"title":"","content":"Disgust would be a good positive-negative pair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T18:41:04-07:00","id":1506568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow?p=1506553#post1506553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't know what to pair with <b>Wonder.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> Boredom? Restlessness? I was thinking it would be something that drives you to seek out wonder. Could be good for a Ironside/Thornside divide.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T09:05:24-07:00","id":1506629,"title":"","content":"Am I really the first person to think of the Lantern Corps?<br /> <br /> Red - Rage<br /> Orange - Greed<br /> Yellow - Fear<br /> Green - Willpower<br /> Blue - Hope<br /> Indigo - Compassion<br /> Violet - Love","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T12:55:31-07:00","id":1506649,"title":"","content":"Wonder could be the opposite of bitterness or suspiction/scepticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T14:50:55-07:00","id":1506660,"title":"","content":"<b>Indigo: </b> Wonder and Delusion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T15:36:45-07:00","id":1506662,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall that in some occultic model, violet was the color of enlightenment, the end of a journey that started from red. I know it's used in representations of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahasrara\" target=\"_blank\">sahasrara</a> for similar purposes, though not as an exact one to one.<br /> <br /> It's been a while since I did some hardcore color theory research, I might get back to you on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T15:46:08-07:00","id":1506663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow?p=1506662#post1506662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall that in some occultic model, violet was the color of enlightenment, the end of a journey that started from red. I know it's used in representations of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahasrara\" target=\"_blank\">sahasrara</a> for similar purposes, though not as an exact one to one.<br /> <br /> It's been a while since I did some hardcore color theory research, I might get back to you on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its from Daoism, its said that when Lao Tze was on his way out of the kingdom and was passing by a westward fortress, a soldier felt violet Qi in the east, which indicated the coming of a sage. Because of this, he made the request that he write down his wisdom, which became the Tao Te Ching. Since then, its seen as an auspicious omen and symbol of enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T17:08:42-07:00","id":1506672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow?p=1506663#post1506663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its from Daoism, its said that when Lao Tze was on his way out of the kingdom and was passing by a westward fortress, a soldier felt violet Qi in the east, which indicated the coming of a sage. Because of this, he made the request that he write down his wisdom, which became the Tao Te Ching. Since then, its seen as an auspicious omen and symbol of enlightenment.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the one I'm thinking is of a definitively more western orientation.<br /> <br /> Still, enough correlation to start spinning something, me thinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T10:48:08-07:00","id":1506765,"title":"","content":"Is there a specific reason why each Color Court has 2 emotions associated with it? The canon Courts all focus on 1 emotion, AFAIK. I think it might be more productive to pick 1 emotion for each Color Court, and elaborate on the sorts of things that the corresponding Courtiers do to ensure there is a steady supply of said emotion. It would also be interesting to elaborate on what happens to the mortals in these Freeholds when the Courtiers harvest too much Glamour from emotions without replanting, so to say.<br /> <br /> For example, let's assume that the Yellow Court is about Curiosity, to avoid excessive overlap with Autumn Court, which is already about fear. The Yellow Court probably makes Pledges with mortals whose professions are linked to education and tourism, in order to cultivate cycles of Curiosity that they can turn into Glamour. But a mortal who suffers a negative Condition because their mind was drained too deeply of Curiosity might start acting more fearfully or callously, which could be an advantage for Autumn and Winter Courts, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T10:55:31-07:00","id":1506766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow?p=1506672#post1506672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the one I'm thinking is of a definitively more western orientation.<br /> <br /> Still, enough correlation to start spinning something, me thinks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this tradition you're thinking of anywhere in <a href=\"https://www.buildingbeautifulsouls.com/symbols-meanings/flower-meanings-symbolism/violet-meaning-symbolism/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this article?</b></a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The flower adapted for a 50th wedding celebration, the Violet\u2019s meaning and symbolism is replete with interesting stories and cultural/religious connotations. <u>Beginning with Christianity, the title Viola odorata means \u201cOur Lady of Modesty\u201d and thus the flower is associated with Mary\u2019s humble nature and her devotion. The story goes that Violets first blossomed when Gabriel told Mary of her son\u2019s impending birth. The Angel Gabriel watches and communicates with humankind, which gives violet another level of potential meaning \u2013 that of protection and connections.</u><br /> <br /> <u>In some sacred art they\u2019re also used to depict a person with deep spiritual insights. These particular association also appeared throughout the Renaissance as part of Classical works.</u> So why the symbolism of modesty? Perhaps because it\u2019s often hard to find the beautiful Violet spirit behind its heart-shaped leaves.<br /> <br /> During the Middle Ages monks called Violets an Herb of the Trinity because they have three primary colors. They also used the folk name of hearts ease because healers had it in their kits for heart disorders. There is no reason we cannot apply this symbolism for emotional struggles as well. Reach out to Violet Spirit when your heart is aching, or when you hope to inspire true love.<br /> <br /> Violets had many uses in the ancient world. They were part of many beauty preparations. <u>Metaphysically you can apply this energy spiritually for personal loveliness or glamour spells.</u><br /> <br /> In Rome violets were common funeral flowers that represent remembrance. Visitors typically carried the flowers with them to safeguard them from air-borne sickness. <u>This custom may tie to the story of Persephone who was picking violets when Pluto took her to the underworld.</u><br /> <br /> Many a traveler used violets to keep their bellies full. The roots, for example, make an excellent soup. To this day violet flowers may be candied and used as edible decorations. In this setting they represent providence.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T13:19:15-07:00","id":1506783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow?p=1506766#post1506766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this tradition you're thinking of anywhere in <a href=\"https://www.buildingbeautifulsouls.com/symbols-meanings/flower-meanings-symbolism/violet-meaning-symbolism/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this article?</b></a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, that's not it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T13:02:55-07:00","id":1507201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1506452-basing-courts-on-the-colors-of-rainbow?p=1506629#post1506629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I really the first person to think of the Lantern Corps?<br /> <br /> Red - Rage<br /> Orange - Greed<br /> Yellow - Fear<br /> Green - Willpower<br /> Blue - Hope<br /> Indigo - Compassion<br /> Violet - Love</div> </div> </div> </div>No you were not. I was thinking the same thing when I saw the op and how it reminded me of that Green Lantern storyline from Geoff Johns.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T14:38:43-07:00","id":1533332,"title":"","content":"<br /> Thread necromancy!<br /> <br /> (just cause I learned this recently while researching a Call of Cthulhu article I wrote)<br /> <br /> In all the talk of the symbolism of violets (the flower of which was quoted a couple of posts ago), there was no mention of its use as a lesbian identifier in the 1920s! Both the flower (and, I think, the color) but also &quot;Violets&quot; was slang for lesbians at the time!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T04:45:32-07:00","id":1536151,"title":"","content":"I just want to object to the indigo/Violet distinction.<br /> <br /> 7 colours of the rainbow were invented to satisfy Newton's occultism. A magic number of colours despite pretty much being able to distinguish 4/5 colours most of the time.<br /> <br /> Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Purple are a fine set of 6 colours if you actually look at a rainbow!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T12:53:06-07:00","id":1536163,"title":"","content":"Yes, but if we're talking magical Courts for Changelings, the occult side is exactly the most important one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}